# Tauri Guidelines

- Keep the frontend and backend responsibilities separated.
- Use Rust for filesystem operations, indexing and core business logic.
- Keep Tauri commands thin.
- Put application logic into dedicated Rust modules.
- Do not expose unnecessary backend functionality to the frontend.
- Validate all data received through IPC.
- Follow Tauri capabilities and permission model.
- Avoid blocking the UI thread with expensive operations.
- Handle filesystem errors explicitly.
- Do not assume that files remain unchanged between operations.